AB  - During medical imaging, images are prone to noise, blur, and motion artifacts due to interference from acquisition equipment or patient breathing and movement, which affects the treatment. At the same time, it is cumbersome and impractical to train individually for different degradation types and levels in applications. Therefore, we propose a generalized medical image restoration network based on prompt multi-granularity attention mechanism. The model prompts degradation information through a prompt attention block with multiple granularities. In single degradation one-by-one tasks, the model enriches multi-scale context information from fine- to coarse-granularity and from low- to high-resolution; In multiple degradation all-in-one tasks, it enables the targeted restoration of each degradation while reducing storage costs. Compared with other advanced methods, our method has the best restoration results on three medical images (including X-ray, Ultrasound Imaging, and Magnetic Resonance Imaging) datasets corresponding to three kinds of degradations (including noise, blur, and motion artifacts). The number of parameters is reduced by 33.40% compared to a prompt learning method (PromptIR: Prompting for All-in-One Blind Image Restoration). The feasibility and performance of restoration of multiple degradation types are demonstrated.
