AB  - Building a high-precision digital twin of power equipment is the key to promoting the digital transformation of the power grid and meeting the demand for modern power professionals. However, existing three-dimensional (3D) reconstruction methods make it difficult to guarantee the required accuracy when processing sparse view inputs, especially in complex outdoor scenes where reconstructing small power equipment poses significant challenges. To address the above challenges, this paper innovatively proposes an accurate sparse view reconstruction method for outdoor small power equipment that combines image enhancement with 3D Gaussian neural field synergy (3DGNF-SPE).The core lies in: (1) using discrete wavelet transform and denoising diffusion probability model to enhance images of small devices under complex lighting occlusion synergistically; (2) Establishing a basic 3D Gaussian representation of the target through the ControlNet++ model of target segmentation, camera pose initialization, and optimization; (3) Constructing learnable neural representations for densification of initial 3D Gaussian elements and performing distillation of normal and depth values; (4) Based on this neural representation, geometric perception sampling is performed, combined with multi-scale Gaussian rendering, to achieve accurate modeling of small power equipment. A large number of experimental verifications have shown that this method achieves significant improvements of 1.01 %, 2.7 %, and 2.1 % in key indicators Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio, Structural Similarity Index Measure, and Learned Perceptual Image Patch Similarity, respectively, and its performance is significantly better than existing mainstream methods. This study effectively solves the problem of high-precision reconstruction of small power equipment in sparse views in complex outdoor environments, providing key technical support for building high-fidelity digital twins of power equipment, supporting intelligent inspection, status assessment, and other intelligent AI applications of the power grid.
